  (D) THE UPSILON LEVER, by re-running the whole pipeline (x1.5 is the mandated step).
      Upsilon_disk    N    rms(canonical)   a_0 at the rms minimum
           0.3333   131          0.1879   5.6234e-11
           0.4000   131          0.1783   7.9433e-11
           0.5000   131          0.1689   1.1220e-10
           0.6000   131          0.1634   1.4125e-10
           0.7500   131          0.1596   2.2387e-10
           0.7000   131          0.1604   1.9953e-10
      d log a_0 / d log Upsilon = +1.7037    (deep-tail rung -0.647; KiDS dwarf lens stack -1.046)
  [FAIL] Upsilon lever |d log a_0/d log Upsilon| < 0.15   (+1.7037)
      AGAINST INTEREST, and a correction to the propose stage: it measured +0.3013 for this lever using
      a per-galaxy weighted fit; the rms-profile estimator here gives +1.70 on the same galaxies and the
      same window.  The lever is therefore itself estimator-dependent by a factor 5.6, which is worse
      than either value: the quantity being levered is not well defined.
      CONSEQUENCE.  Stellar populations know Upsilon_[3.6] to about 0.09 dex, so at lever +1.70 the
      Upsilon systematic on a_0 is 0.15 dex, on top of the 0.125 dex statistical error.
      Total 0.20 dex -- the two footings are 0.082 dex apart,
      so this estimator cannot see the difference it was built to see.

  (E) THE STRICTLY UPSILON-FREE FORM.  Where the outer window really is point-mass-like the baryonic
      slope is -2 by geometry, no photometry enters, and the Upsilon lever is EXACTLY 0.  This is the
      only version of the candidate that meets its own advertisement, so it is run as the primary.
      N = 38 galaxies with dln g_bar/dln r in [-2.25, -1.75]
      rms(canonical) 0.1442   correlation observed-vs-predicted r = +0.236   regression 0.709
      a_0 from this Upsilon-free subsample: 4.467e-10  (log10 -9.3500 +- 0.2925 galaxy bootstrap)
      that is +0.68 dex from canonical and +0.60 dex from alt.
  [FAIL] the Upsilon-free form recovers a_0 within 0.3 dex of a footing   (a_0 = 4.467e-10)
  [FAIL] the Upsilon-free form correlates with the prediction at r > 0.5   (r = +0.236)

